id: pm-gh1667
title: "GH-1667: sdk/graph does not export ProjectedGraphResult, the public return type of runGraph, and the merge conflict_resolution union has no public name, so extensions derive both"
description: "GitHub issue #1667 (reported 2026-11-04 against 2026.11.4, TypeScript NodeNext, strict, skipLibCheck false). import type { ProjectedGraphResult } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/graph' and import type { MergeConflictResolution } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/merge' both fail with TS2305. Source confirms it: ProjectedGraphResult is exported from src/sdk/graph/run.ts and is the declared return type of runGraph, but src/sdk/graph/index.ts re-exports runGraph from run.js through a named list that omits the type, and sdk/public-surface.json records runGraph's signature as returning ProjectedGraphResult while the type itself is not on the surface. MergeDecisionReceipt in src/sdk/merge/receipts.ts types conflict_resolution inline with no public alias. Two fleet packages, pm-graph and pm-brief, independently derive the names with Awaited<ReturnType<typeof runGraph>> and an indexed access on MergeDecisionReceipt. Expected: ProjectedGraphResult is re-exported from sdk/graph and the aggregate entrypoint, the merge resolution union has a public name that the receipt declaration uses, and the SDK surface acceptance covers type-only imports next to the value-export parity checks. Why it matters for agents and extension authors: derived aliases break silently when the internal shape moves, and every extension author repeats the workaround. Related closed work covers values only: pm-obbh43 (GH-740) made the aggregate barrel complete for value exports of declared subpaths, and pm-suhxny derived the surface denominator from the export map, but neither checks that a type named in a public signature is itself importable. Duplicate check: searched SDK named type exports, ProjectedGraphResult, type-only surface acceptance, MergeDecisionReceipt and the aggregate entrypoint across all statuses, and no item owns missing public type names."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,extensions,"gh:1667",sdk,types
