comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T09:04:28.169Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence (branch feat/extension-authoring-contracts, 2026-11-07).\n\nMeasured the gap on the emitted declarations with the TypeScript checker: 281 entrypoint x type gaps, 197 distinct package types named by exported function signatures (parameters, return types, type-parameter constraints) that the entrypoint did not export: ./sdk 120, ./sdk/testing 41, ./sdk/runtime 39, ./sdk/core 24, ./sdk/query 20, ./sdk/authoring 14, ./sdk/governance 11, ./sdk/graph 7 (including ProjectedGraphResult for runGraph), ./sdk/contracts 3, ./sdk/merge 2. HistoryEntry (named by appendHistoryEntry) was exported from no entrypoint at all.\n\nChange:\n- scripts/sdk-surface-snapshot.mjs: analyzeSignatureTypeReachability walks every exported function declaration's signature, resolves each type reference to its declaration, and reports package types (declared under dist/) the same entrypoint does not export. Identity is by declaration, so a same-named different type is still a gap. buildSdkSurfaceSnapshot refuses any gap, naming the type, its declaration file and the functions that name it, and the snapshot records signature_type_reachability counts per entrypoint.\n- Closed all 281 gaps with type-only re-exports per entrypoint, plus export keywords on 27 module-local types (for example ReadPromise, ReadOptions, InitialReadOptions in runtime.ts; AcquireLockOptions in core/lock).\n- sdk/extension-contracts ExtensionCapability re-exports the structurally identical core declaration, so signatures typed with the core alias resolve to the exported type.\n- The merge half already held: MergeDecisionReceipt.conflict_resolution is typed by the exported ItemScalarConflictResolution, importable from sdk/merge and the aggregate; the type test now imports it from both.\n- tests/types/sdk-subpath-entrypoints.test-d.ts imports ProjectedGraphResult (sdk/graph and sdk), ItemScalarConflictResolution and MergeDecisionReceipt (sdk/merge), HistoryEntry (sdk) and ExtensionActivationResult (sdk/testing) as type-only imports beside the value-export parity checks.\n\nSDK surface: 306 classified changes, all additive or compatible except four acknowledged signature changes (CliFlagContract gains optional owner/sdk_option in ./sdk and ./sdk/contracts; ExtensionCapability now names the core declaration in ./sdk and ./sdk/authoring).\n\nVerified: tests/unit/scripts/sdk-surface-snapshot.spec.ts (19 tests) covers gaps, identity, unresolved names, merged function+namespace, and the build refusal. Negative control: deleting the ProjectedGraphResult re-export from dist/sdk/graph.d.ts makes sdk-surface-snapshot --check fail with './sdk/graph: ProjectedGraphResult (declared in dist/sdk/graph/run.d.ts; named by runGraph)'.\n\nFollow-up filed: pm-bqyk1z (98 class-member and 875 type-declaration references still name unexported types; mostly PmClient methods from ./sdk/core).\n"
  "2026-11-07T10:00:02.250Z","harness:claude-code","Codex round 1 on the batch: the signature gate now also checks exported variable annotations (callable values such as runUpdateMany) and resolves inline import type qualifiers; eight more gaps closed. Details on pm-gh1665."
